    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d421">

                <pb facs="0325" n="321" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg321"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.61331/103: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tsingtao</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gourley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tsingtao</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-14T14:00:00+08:00">May 14, 1938—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Embassy’s April 15, 2 p.m.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d421-f1"/> Conditions along the
                    railway between Tsingtao and Tsinanfu have greatly improved since April and
                    trains are again running regularly. Japanese officials have promised
                    British-American Tobacco Company protection for its tobacco buyers. Officials of
                    the company who recently went into interior consider the situation much better.
                    Eleven American citizen tobacco buyers are among those who intend to go to
                    Ershihlipu on May 24, 25 and 26. No assistance or advice has been requested from
                    this Consulate and unless the Department instructs otherwise no advice against
                    taking risks will be voluntarily given to individual buyers. An official of the
                    company states that the company would not let the men go if it were considered
                    unsafe and believes it would needlessly frighten them if the Consulate should
                    now advise them against taking risks.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gourley</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d421-f1" n="15" xml:id="d421-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably repeating the Department’s telegram No. 106, April 14, 4 p.m., <ref
                        target="#pg309">p. 309</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
